 "file": "CDROM/TAIIKU/TAMA.BIN",
 "note": "Sports day, ball roll: the course-out banner (コース / アウト, two 128x64 sprites that slide across the screen when the ball leaves the course; drawn with tpage (832,256) 8 bpp, CLUT (0,511)). TAIIKU .BIN files are 8-bpp 128x128 pages from file offset 0x2000; コース is the bottom half of page 17 (0x46000, rows 64..127), アウト the top half of page 18 (0x4A000, rows 0..63; GOAL below it is kept). The CLUT the banner is drawn with is not TAMA.BIN's own: it is row 15 of the 16-row CLUT block of TASETU.BIN (0x1E00), a 15-step cyan-to-blue ramp in indices 1..15 (traced 2026-11-03 from the GP0 log: SPRT clut 0x7FC0; the VRAM row matches TASETU.BIN byte for byte). The English is the 12-px Latin font at scale 4 (each font pixel a 4x4 block; 5 would need the 1-px squeeze, which joins the letters) with the ramp top to bottom and a ring in the darkest index. English DRAFT. Name plates (cells plate_*, \"mirror\"): six of the same 32x16 surname plates as KARI.BIN's, stored left-right reversed: page 14 (0x3A000) row 112 (藤崎 at x 32) and page 15 (0x3E000) x 0..63 rows 0..63. A seventh, 紐緒 (page 14 x 0..31 row 112), is half overwritten (x 0..15 holds other art) and is left as it is. No frame of the ball roll draws them; English as in KARI, rendered mirrored.",
